      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To get started with GridDeploy, ensure your AWS credentials are configured in `~/.aws/credentials`, Docker is running, and a `grid.yaml` file exists in your project root. First, create your deployment configuration file named `grid.yaml` in the root directory to define your environment variables and resource specifications. Next, authenticate by logging into the AWS console or using the `aws configure` command to link your local profile to your account. Finally, run the CLI command `gd deploy --env production --config grid.yaml` to initiate the deployment process to your target environment. This guide covers all necessary prerequisites and steps to deploy your application efficiently using the official GridDeploy tool.",
